{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Beside his sales to the fathers.</b> It was not for the fathers to apportion priestly watches, but only his sales — that is, what each watch was able to sell to another in exchange: the offerings of all the days of the year, where each watch would exchange with its fellows its share in the year's offerings for what they would give him of their share in one week or two. But the festival offerings, which cannot be exchanged and are not included among his sales that the fathers could apportion into watches — therefore <b>they shall eat a portion equal to a portion</b> of them."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:21:43.335176707Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}